      "committer": {
        "name": "Marc Britten",
        "email": "11667518+marcbritten@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-23T10:58:03Z"
      },
      "message": "Merge remote-tracking branch 'upstream/main' into issue/3609-read-only-open\n\nMain now has #3608 (overwrite guard) and #3584 (start options). Both sides\nadded lines in the same places. The merge keeps both sides:\n\n- The save path checks read-only first, then the overwrite guard. Thus\n  `overwrite: true` does not write over a file that is open read-only.\n- `LiveOptions` and `Env` have `read_only` and `doc_stamp`.\n- `save_project` has the two sentences, and `open_project` has `read_only?`.\n- `run_windowed` takes the start mode and `read_only`.\n- `cli_options.rs` is main's file (LF line ends) with the `--read-only` option.\n- Two test literals get the field of the other change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
